      <p class="text-theme-primary text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Quick answer:</strong> <a href="/anping-wire-mesh/" class="text-theme-primary underline">Anping wire mesh</a> is cheap for honest structural reasons: a 60-year industrial cluster of 500+ factories with shared everything—labor, wire rod supply, galvanizing capacity, logistics—and ferocious local competition the Chinese call 内卷 (neijuan, involution), where overcapacity pushes margins to 3–8%. Most low quotes are simply the cluster working as designed. But a quote that is 20–30% below the market is almost always a trap built on three tricks: <strong>thin wire</strong> (undersized by 0.02–0.05 mm), <strong>light zinc</strong> (180 g/m² shipped as "hot-dip 275"), and <strong>narrow width</strong> (a 2.0 m roll cut at 1.95 m). All three are caught in minutes with a scale and the <a href="/tools/welded-wire-mesh-weight-calculator/" class="text-theme-primary underline">weight calculator</a>—verify before you pay, not after the container arrives.
      </p>
