        Every importer of <a href="/wire-mesh-hebei/" class="text-theme-accent hover:underline">Hebei wire mesh</a> eventually asks the same question: is this quote too cheap to be true? Usually the answer is no—Anping genuinely is the lowest-cost place on earth to make welded and woven wire mesh, and Western wholesale prices of $1–2/m² for products that cost $0.30–0.50/m² FOB reflect distribution margins, not hidden flaws. But the same cluster dynamics that create honest low prices also reward a minority of factories for quietly selling you less steel and less zinc than you paid for. Understanding both sides of that equation is the core skill of buying from Anping.
      </p>
