              <td class="p-3">Electro-galv passed as HDG</td>
              <td class="p-3">Coating gauge + strip test</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 font-medium">Quote refuses to state zinc g/m²</td>
              <td class="p-3">Light zinc</td>
              <td class="p-3">Demand number + ASTM A90 method in contract</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 font-medium">Roll weight quoted, never length/width checked</td>
              <td class="p-3">Narrow width / short length</td>
              <td class="p-3">Physical tape measure on 3 rolls per container</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-medium">CIF quote 20% below FOB-equivalent peers</td>
              <td class="p-3">Freight padding over cheap product</td>
              <td class="p-3">FOB price calculator normalization</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="text-theme-secondary mb-4">
        The broader protection is structural: 3–5 comparable quotes, a verified supplier (see our <a href="/blog/how-to-verify-china-wire-mesh-factory/" class="text-theme-accent hover:underline">factory verification guide</a>), samples approved in writing, 30/70 payment terms, and inspection before the balance. Cheap mesh from Anping is a genuine gift of industrial geography—if your paperwork makes cheating more expensive than honesty.
      </p>
